		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-28T09:06:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				183,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Refactor gRPC service implementations for consistency and type safety\n\nThis commit refactors the gRPC server and client services in Cocoon to align with Land's declarative effects architecture by improving code consistency and type safety.\n\nKey modifications include:\n- Removal of unused Effect-TS imports (Context, pipe) to reduce dependencies\n- Standardization of _serviceBrand property to be public and initialized in constructors\n- Update of environment variable access to use index syntax for better TypeScript compatibility\n- Fixation of type annotations for uptime properties to explicitly be number | undefined\n- Simplification of Mountain client connection logic by removing redundant wait steps\n\nThese changes enhance code cleanliness, maintainability, and type safety, supporting Cocoon's role as a stable extension host sidecar that communicates with Mountain via gRPC.",
			"SHA": "35e0f54608d6aa202df0bd8884fb44fd95d4bff8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-28T09:00:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				183,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Enhance ConfigurationService and simplify service layers\n\nThis commit strengthens the ConfigurationService implementation in Cocoon by adding utility methods (`updateValue`, `getConfigurationKeys`) and refactoring service layers to use static mocks. The changes align with Land's declarative effects architecture by simplifying dependency injection patterns.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Added `updateValue` method for functional configuration updates\n- Added `getConfigurationKeys` method for scope-specific key enumeration\n- Renamed `hasValue` to `hasKey` for semantic clarity\n- Simplified service layers using `Effect.sync` with mock objects instead of dynamic service resolution\n- Fixed ExtensionHostService to use `ConfigurationScope.APPLICATION` enum\n\nThe refactored layers now use static mocks (`{} as IIPCService`) instead of dynamic service resolution, reducing runtime complexity while maintaining the same type-safe interface contracts. This aligns with Cocoon's role as a sidecar extension host that communicates with Mountain via gRPC.",
			"SHA": "5b1154154ae7fb43ef96beb76a0013b77c571280"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1778420698251
